  "meta": {
    "name": "Time Smear",
    "createdAt": "2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z",
    "modifiedAt": "2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "ts_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -314
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Time smear\n\nA star (Curve in `star` mode) spins once a loop while two LFOs swing it across the canvas in a figure of eight. The Shader's `history` is 48: it keeps the input's last 48 frames on the GPU, and the GLSL reads them back with iHistoryFrame(ago, uv) (0 = now). Each band of rows shows a different moment, the delay rolling down the picture in a wave, and now and then a block jumps further back: the motion smears and tears like a datamoshed video.\n\nOpen the Shader panel to edit it; `bands`, `glitch` and `background` are uniforms.",
        "width": 480,
        "height": 250
      },
      "portValues": {
        "text": "Time smear\n\nA star (Curve in `star` mode) spins once a loop while two LFOs swing it across the canvas in a figure of eight. The Shader's `history` is 48: it keeps the input's last 48 frames on the GPU, and the GLSL reads them back with iHistoryFrame(ago, uv) (0 = now). Each band of rows shows a different moment, the delay rolling down the picture in a wave, and now and then a block jumps further back: the motion smears and tears like a datamoshed video.\n\nOpen the Shader panel to edit it; `bands`, `glitch` and `background` are uniforms.",
        "width": 480,
        "height": 250
      }
    },
